<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 AngrySandhill
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

SignPath doesn't read this file. It is a copy, kept here for review, of the artifact configuration entered in
the SignPath project under the slug "uninstaller", which .github/workflows/release.yml names when it sends
Inno Setup's uninstaller; change the two together. build.py uninstaller-out uploads that uninst-*.e32 as
uninstaller.exe, because SignPath's pe-file reference lists .exe and not .e32. Inno Setup writes the same
version information into it as into Setup, so it carries the same restriction as installer.xml: the product
name Tapewright and the version release.yml passes. upload-artifact zips what it uploads, so the root is a
zip-file.
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="version" required="true" />
  </parameters>
  <zip-file>
    <pe-file path="uninstaller.exe" product-name="Tapewright" product-version="${version}">
      <authenticode-sign />
    </pe-file>
  </zip-file>
</artifact-configuration>
